Inspiration
-----------
The idea of pairing a direction method for motion graphics with scripts that check the rendered film was
inspired by the open-source project "motionmaxxing" (https://github.com/Tejashmakwana/motionmaxxing),
licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

motionproof is an independent implementation written from scratch. It contains no source code, text,
data, fonts, images or third-party libraries from that project. Its scripts, runtime, rules, thresholds,
references and test fixtures are original work.

Third-party software
--------------------
None is bundled. At run time motionproof calls programs installed on the user's machine: Node.js,
Python, FFmpeg and, for HTML films only, a Chromium-based browser (Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge).
